       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults in a monitored setting. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day), the usual range for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, confirm that and give me the clinical rationale for the order note. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
