       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. I know you've confirmed it, and you're the one making the clinical decisions. But 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled dose, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. Extra ibuprofen above the ceiling adds toxicity (GI bleeding, kidney injury, cardiovascular events) without adding benefit. You also haven't given a rationale, and an order like this could be given before anyone catches it.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- **Enter 800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum dose. I can add a note such as \"max dose; monitor renal function and GI symptoms.\"\n- **Enter a lower dose** if you want one, such as 400\u2013600 mg four times daily.\n- **Enter it with a different drug** if the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect. I can help you think through options like scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen, or other agents.\n\nIf you believe a dose above the maximum is truly needed, please talk to pharmacy or your attending first. Once that's settled, you or they can place the order directly. Do you want me to enter one of the options above?"
      }
